      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\r\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\r\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"4\">Level 4 - Advanced</span>\r\n    <span class=\"time\">40 min</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip accent\">Coding</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip\">Deep dive</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip\">Graphs</span>\r\n  </div>\r\n  <h1>Weighted Shortest Paths: Dijkstra, Bellman-Ford and Floyd-Warshall</h1>\r\n  <p class=\"lead\">When edges have costs, BFS stops being enough. This page builds Dijkstra from a burning-fuse picture up to the heap version with the stale-entry check, then covers the variants interviewers actually ask: minimax paths, \"at most K stops\", counting shortest paths and all-pairs tables. You get four tested templates, two animations and a one-glance chart for picking the right algorithm.</p>\r\n"
